{
  "_comment": [
    "month-rollup.json - the monthly table's cap.",
    "",
    "Sheet one of the report has room for a bounded number of table rows, and the",
    "monthly table was the only part with no bound. MonthRollup keeps the most",
    "recent six months in full and folds everything older into one summary row.",
    "",
    "The summary's average is the summed grams over the summed effectiveDays, NOT",
    "the mean of the monthly averages: a 31-day month and a 3-day month do not",
    "weigh the same. That is the case a reimplementation gets wrong, and the",
    "seven- and eight-month cases are where the cap starts to bite.",
    "",
    "Both suites load this file: Android MonthRollup.capped, iOS the same name."
  ],
